|~ qlang operand catalog — format family. Each operand BindStep
   below sits directly under the per-site error tags it raises;
   the operand's `:throws` Vec references those tags by name. ~|

:json
  |~~ Renders the subject as a JSON string. qlang-only shapes
      lose round-trip identity at this boundary: a keyword becomes
      its bare name, a key and a value alike (`:foo` → `"foo"`), Sets
      flatten to arrays, Maps emit their keys as object keys. Use
      this for handing values to non-qlang consumers; for in-pipeline
      pretty-printing reach for `pretty`.

      ~({:a 1 :b 2} | json | eq "{\"a\":1,\"b\":2}")
      ~([:foo :bar] | json | eq "[\"foo\",\"bar\"]")
      ~(#[1 2 3] | json | eq "[1,2,3]")
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/json
            :category :format
            :subject :any
            :returns :string
   }

:parseJson
  |~~ Parses a String of plain JSON into a qlang value, the reverse
      of `json`. Object keys become qlang keywords; arrays become
      Vecs; scalars pass through. Lossy with respect to qlang-only
      types — a Set arriving from JSON looks like a Vec, a keyword
      as a value cannot be told from a String, error values have no
      plain-JSON form. Use this for input from any producer that
      speaks JSON.

      ~("42" | parseJson | eq 42)
      ~("\"hello\"" | parseJson | eq "hello")
      ~("[1,2,3]" | parseJson | eq [1 2 3])
      ~("{\"name\":\"alice\"}" | parseJson | eq {:name "alice"})
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/parseJson
            :category :format
            :subject :string
            :returns :any
            :modifiers []}

::ParseJsonSubjectNotStringError
  |~~ Subject of `parseJson` must be a String — the raw JSON text;
      a value renders to one through `json` first.

      ~(
        42 | parseJson
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::ParseJsonSubjectNotStringError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

::ParseJsonInvalidJsonError
  |~~ `parseJson` could not parse the subject as JSON. The message
      of the host's parser rides on `:message`.

      ~("{not json" | parseJson !| type | eq ::ParseJsonInvalidJsonError)
  ~~|
